// §14 entry 20 -- CRLF line ending -> EXS-E0106.
//
// §8.1: "LF only. CRLF is EXS-E0106. The formatter converts; the
// compiler does not." One line below ends CRLF (\r\n) instead of LF,
// deliberately -- everything up to and including that line is otherwise
// exactly saluta.exsc's own opening function.
//
// THIS FILE DELIBERATELY CONTAINS THE VIOLATION IT TESTS -- see entry 3's
// fixture for why a CRLF here is not a §8.1 self-application violation
// of this project's own source (this file IS the test input, not the tool;
// every OTHER line in this file is plain LF, including this directive).
//
// lexer/source.inc's §8.1 pass STOPS at the first CR (its own header:
